    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're suggesting that there's a distinct physiological \"shorthand\" that the market uses to categorize these two different levels of luxury. \n\nTo make sure I'm following your logic for the creative team: you essentially seem to be saying that certain physical traits—like the ones you've linked to \"mass-premium\" energy—are fundamentally at odds with the \"intellectual\" prestige we're trying to build. \n\nIf we were to, say, cast a model with more \"vibrant\" or \"bold\" features (the darker skin tones or more athletic builds you mentioned) but place them in a very minimalist, high-culture setting, would that help bridge the gap, or would the physical characteristics themselves still trigger a \"mass-market\" perception in the eyes of our ultra-high-net-worth target? Basically, is the perceived \"lack of refinement\" tied more to the setting and styling, or is it an inherent association with those specific physical archetypes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
